    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "body_html": "<ul class=\"do\"><li>Have the cooked rice ready, covered, and cool it only until comfortable to hold. Wet your hands and rub a little salt over both palms.</li><li>Fold the prepared eggplant evenly through <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"480\" data-b=\"720\" data-s=\"0\">480–720 g</span> warm rice. Divide into four to six portions, about <span class=\"q\" data-k=\"mass\" data-u=\"g\" data-a=\"120\" data-s=\"0\">120 g</span> rice per onigiri before adding the eggplant. There is no separate filling pocket.</li><li>Cup the rice from below with one hand. Bend the other hand into a roof, press gently to make a corner, turn a third of a turn and repeat. Keep it loose: press only enough to hold together.</li></ul>",
   "heat": null,
